    {
      "id": "pipeline",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "# Truth Project Pipeline\n\n**Phase 0:** Source Acquisition\n17 books → plaintext (19MB)\n\n**Phase 1:** Chapter Notes\n`obsidian-book-notes` skill\n149 notes, ~466KB\nClaim → Evidence → Confidence\n\n**Phase 2:** Claims Extraction\n`extract-loop.sh` + `claims-extraction`\nLLM + human-in-the-loop\n380+ claims, typed edges\n\n**Phase 3:** Knowledge Graph\nObsidian graph view\nQueryable by topic, scholar,\nevidence, confidence\n\n**Phase 4:** Synthesis (pending)\nArgument dependency maps\nConvergence scoring\nFault-line detection\n\n---\n**Notes:** [[notes/pipeline-overview]]\n**Claims:** [[notes/claims-architecture]]"
    },
    {
      "id": "orkg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 420,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# ORKG\nOpen Research Knowledge Graph\n\n**(Auer, D'Souza, Farfar et al.)**\nLeibniz University Hannover\nSince ~2019\n\n## Same Pipeline Architecture\n\n**Ingestion:** LLM + human-in-loop\npapers → structured claims\n\n**Structuring:** Semantic\nfrontmatter on claim nodes\n\n**Enrichment:** Typed edges\nbetween claims (cross-paper)\n\n**Synthesis:** Evidence synthesis\nfrom graph structure\n\n## Key References\n\nAuer et al. (2025) — flagship\n20+ citations\n\nTan & D'Souza (2026) — LLM\nextraction for meta-analysis\n\nAggarwal (2026) — human-in-\nloop extraction model\n\n---\n**Full analysis:** [[methodology-alignment]]"
    },
    {
      "id": "convergence",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 210,
      "y": 540,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "# Independent Convergence\n\nBoth pipelines developed organically\n— no prior knowledge of each other.\n\n**Same pattern:**\nstructured claims → typed edges →\ngraph querying → synthesis\n\n**Key difference:**\nORKG = millions of papers, shallow\nTruth = 17 books, deep per-chapter\n\n**Implication:** The pattern is robust.\nIndependent arrival = methodological\nvalidity, not coincidence.\n\n[[methodology-alignment]]"
    },
